say why a delayed perform was scheduled, not just that it fired

A delayed perform runs with its scheduling stack long gone, so a backtrace at fire time names only
the run loop. That is what made #210 hard: iA Writer undoes its own table selection from one, and
nothing in the process could say why.

Two traces, both on CIDER_TRACE_PERFORM.

At FIRE time the selector is the whole identity of the work, so it prints target class and selector.
Twenty one fire in an iA Writer launch and exactly one is the interesting one:

  CIDER_PERFORM fire NSKVONotifying_Writer.LibraryTreeViewController -> deselectSelectedRow:

At SCHEDULE time the stack is still live and carries the reason. An unfiltered backtrace per perform
buries the answer, so the variable doubles as a filter: set it to a substring of the selector and
only matching schedules print a stack. CIDER_TRACE_PERFORM=deselect gave the whole chain:

  CIDER_PERFORM schedule ... -> deselectSelectedRow: delay=0.05
    4 AppKit           -[NSApplication sendAction:to:from:]
    5 AppKitAdditions  -[IATableView mouseDown:] + 460
    6 AppKit           -[NSWindow sendEvent:]

which is the application deselecting from its own action handler, not anything this AppKit did.

--- a/src/NSRunLoop.m
+++ b/src/NSRunLoop.m
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@
 #import <Foundation/NSTimer.h>
 #import "CFInternal.h"
 #import <libkern/OSAtomic.h>
+#import <objc/runtime.h>
+#include <execinfo.h>
+#include <string.h>
 
 CF_EXPORT CFTypeRef _CFRunLoopGet2(CFRunLoopRef rl); //locking version
 CF_EXPORT CFTypeRef _CFRunLoopGet2b(CFRunLoopRef rl); //non locking version
@@ -379,6 +382,14 @@
 static void __NSFireDelayedPerform(CFRunLoopTimerRef timer, void *info)
 {
     NSDelayedPerformer *performer = (NSDelayedPerformer *)info;
+    /* A delayed perform runs with the scheduling stack long gone, so a backtrace here names only the
+     * run loop. The selector is the whole identity of the work. See the schedule side below, which
+     * is where a reason can still be read. */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_PERFORM") != NULL && getenv("CIDER_TRACE_PERFORM")[0] != '\0') {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_PERFORM fire %s -> %s\n", object_getClassName(performer->object),
+                sel_getName(performer->selector));
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
     @autoreleasepool {
         [performer->object performSelector:performer->selector withObject:performer->argument];
     }
@@ -396,6 +407,23 @@
               afterDelay: (NSTimeInterval) delay
                  inModes: (NSArray<NSRunLoopMode> *) modes
 {
+    /* WHY a delayed perform was asked for is only readable HERE. Set CIDER_TRACE_PERFORM to a
+     * substring of the selector to get the scheduling stack for just that one; an unfiltered
+     * backtrace per perform buries the answer, since a launch schedules dozens. */
+    const char *want = getenv("CIDER_TRACE_PERFORM");
+    if (want != NULL && want[0] != '\0' && strstr(sel_getName(aSelector), want) != NULL) {
+        void *frames[24];
+        int count = backtrace(frames, 24);
+        char **names = backtrace_symbols(frames, count);
+
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_PERFORM schedule %s -> %s delay=%g\n", object_getClassName(self),
+                sel_getName(aSelector), delay);
+        for (int i = 1; i < count && names != NULL; i++)
+            fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_PERFORM schedule   %s\n", names[i]);
+        free(names);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
+
     NSRunLoop *rl = [NSRunLoop currentRunLoop];
     CFRunLoopRef loop = [rl getCFRunLoop];
 
